# The proportions of a drawn, large-headed body: the avatar body with the ranges its drawn sheets need
law avatar_body_stylised
kind proportion
derive avatar_body body.law
claim the body of avatar_body, with the ranges of drawn sheets (n=2) where the sheets were measured; every other parameter keeps the range of avatar_body
claim a measured range = each sheet's value with its measurement ± (pixel picks on the sheet), widened by the calibration floor of picks against 3D bodies (knee +0.021 correction applied, ±0.003; landmark heights ±0.006) and rounded outward to 2 decimals; the default is the sheets' mean rounded to 2 decimals
claim knee and face_length are measured on both sheets, shoulder on one: two sheets are a floor for the range, not its envelope
param knee number = 0.32 range 0.27 0.38
param face_length number = 0.07 range 0.06 0.08
# the shoulder is a fixed let in avatar_body; a drawn sheet puts it lower
param shoulder number = 0.88 range 0.86 0.9
